From f281d7611ec7b7fa7f77fa9db14bede32b49ef31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 12:12:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rtrafd/webui: v1.3.3 - live Traffic Analyzer (1s dual-cadence
 collector + rolling live view), poll-rate selector, settings-scroll fix

Live view was frozen: the daemon sampled every 30s and the page drew the
charts once from history without refreshing.

Daemon (dual cadence):
- POLL 30 -> 1s base tick drives WAN rate + live.json every second. Per-class
  polled every 2 ticks (tmctl is heavier than a proc read); the flow-cache
  scan (per-device/per-network/top-talkers) and ping probe run every 5 ticks
  to keep CPU down. History rings just accumulate finer deltas into the same
  5-min/hour/day slots.
- Live rate holders (lv_wan/lv_cls/lv_cli/lv_net) computed at each source's
  cadence and republished into live.json every tick; write_live now emits
  per-network and per-device live rates ("net"/"dev") so those panels update
  without waiting on the 5-min history file. top_note rate now divided by the
  flow-cache interval (FCACHE_SECS), not the base tick.

webui:
- Live window: rolling WAN line chart + rolling per-class stacked (client-side
  buffers, ~2 min) + live per-network bars + live per-device rate table, all
  refreshed on the live poll. History windows unchanged.
- Refresh-rate selector (1s/10s/30s, persisted in localStorage) controls the
  live poll interval; restarts the timer on change.
- Settings button now scrollIntoView()s the settings panel - the page runs in
  the shell's auto-grown iframe (inner window doesn't scroll), so the old
  scrollTo() was a no-op.

Mock-validated (rolling charts, net/dev panels, selector, settings scroll).
EXTENDNO=Reaper_v1.3.3. Metal test: WAN graph ticks ~1s; class/net/device
update live; selector changes cadence; Settings scrolls; watch CPU with the
1s tick (class cadence + selector are the dials).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
